   "id": 631743,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "<p dir=\"ltr\">The graph below represents the temperature, <span data-math=\"t(m)\">t(m)</span>, in degrees Fahrenheit of water used for a cup of hot tea over time in minutes, <span data-math=\"m\">m</span>. What does <span data-math=\"t(0)\">t(0)</span> represent?&nbsp;</p>\n<p dir=\"ltr\"><strong><img alt=\"GRAPH THAT SHOWS TEMPERATURE IN DEGREES FAHRENHEIT AS A FUNCTION OF TIME IN MINUTES WITH A \\(y\\)-intercepts OF 70. THE GRAPH INCREASES, THEN DECREASES, AND THEN REMAINS CONSTANT.\" class=\"img-fluid atto_image_button_text-bottom\" height=\"299\" src=\"exercises/media/266a099a7945ec24.jpg\" width=\"300\"></strong><br></p>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1222582,
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"t(0)= 180\">t(0)= 180</span>; After 180 minutes, the temperature is 0 degrees."
    },
    {
     "id": 1222583,
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"t(0)=70\">t(0)=70</span>; After 0 minutes, the temperature is 70 degrees."
    },
    {
